.TH tuflow n 0.4 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuflow
.PP
The front end of the \fBtuflow\fR diagram family: it parses a Mermaid / flowchart source block and renders it to SVG or PNG. It is the single entry point a consumer (e.g. a documentation renderer) calls; it detects the diagram kind and dispatches to the right family module, so the caller never has to know whether a block is a graph, a class diagram or a pie chart.
.PP
Everything is pure Tcl: graphs go through \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (a node\-edge layout over the \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR / \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR backends). Pie charts, xy charts, sequences, gantt charts and the other non\-graph families each have their own module. No Tk, no browser, no external rasteriser.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuflow 0.4
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuflow::parse    text                       ;# -> tudiagram model (graphs only)
::tclutils::tuflow::toSvg     text ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> SVG string
::tclutils::tuflow::toPng     text ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tuflow::writeSvg  text file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (SVG)
::tclutils::tuflow::writePng  text file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (PNG)
.CE
.PP
\fBwriteSvg\fR and \fBwritePng\fR write through a temporary file (\fBcommon::replaceFile\fR): a failed write leaves the old file and no open channel (tclutils 0.69.0).
.PP
\fBparse\fR is \fBgraph\-only\fR: it returns a \fBtudiagram\fR model for the graph\-like Mermaid types and raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUFLOW UNSUPPORTED}\fR for every non\-graph type, including ones that \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR draw. \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR are the \fBrender facade\fR: they detect a non\-graph block before \fBparse\fR is reached and dispatch it to that family's renderer.
.PP
\fBwriteSvg\fR and \fBwritePng\fR pass their options through to \fBtoSvg\fR and \fBtoPng\fR. A key the facade does not forward for that diagram is dropped.
.SS Graphs
.PP
\fBtoPng\fR / \fBwritePng\fR accept:
.CS
-scale N       positive integer, default 1
               PNG supersample; the layout stays on the 6x8 metric
-fontfile F    TTF or OTF for the labels
.CE
.PP
\fBtoSvg\fR / \fBwriteSvg\fR take no options. \fB\-scale\fR and \fB\-fontfile\fR are dropped. The SVG text uses the viewer's \fBmonospace\fR.
.PP
\fB\-fontfile\fR is stored on the model with \fBtudiagram::setMeta\fR and read when the PNG is drawn. The file must exist; a missing path is \fB{TCLUTILS TUDIAGRAM FONT}\fR. The outline font comes from the unbundled \fBGlyphs\fR package. If that package is missing, the labels stay the 6x8 bitmap and no error is raised. \fB\-width\fR, \fB\-height\fR and \fB\-legend\fR are dropped on a graph.
.SS "Other families"
.PP
\fBtoSvg\fR and \fBtoPng\fR both forward:
.CS
-width N       canvas width in pixels
-height N      canvas height in pixels
-scale N       positive integer, default 1
-fontfile F    TTF or OTF, PNG only
-legend 0|1    pie only, default 1
.CE
.PP
\fB\-scale\fR must be a positive integer. On PNG the canvas is \fB\-width\fR times \fB\-scale\fR by \fB\-height\fR times \fB\-scale\fR, and the family uses the same number as its drawing scale. On SVG the canvas stays at \fB\-width\fR by \fB\-height\fR. \fB\-fontfile\fR is ignored on SVG. On PNG a missing file is a \fBFONT\fR error from that family (\fB{TCLUTILS TUPIE FONT}\fR and the same shape for the others). A missing \fBGlyphs\fR package keeps the bitmap font.
.PP
Defaults when the option is left out:
.CS
pie               -width 480  -height 320  -legend 1
xychart-beta      -width 520  -height 340
quadrantChart     -width 420  -height 420
journey           -width 600  -height 360
timeline          -width 640  -height 380
sankey            -width 700  -height 400
gantt             -width 800  -height 0     0 = 400, or more for many tasks
sequenceDiagram   -width 0    -height 0     0 = size from the layout
radar             -width 600  -height 600
treemap           -width 640  -height 400
packet            -width 640  -height 0     0 = height from the row count
kanban            -width 0    -height 0     0 = size from columns and cards
.CE
.PP
\fBsankey\-beta\fR, \fBradar\-beta\fR, \fBtreemap\-beta\fR and \fBpacket\-beta\fR use the same defaults as the name without \fB\-beta\fR. \fB\-legend 0\fR draws the pie without the legend column.
.SS "Flowchart syntax (parse)"
.IP \(bu
Header \fBgraph\fR or \fBflowchart\fR with an optional direction \fBLR\fR, \fBRL\fR, \fBTB\fR, \fBTD\fR (= \fBTB\fR) or \fBBT\fR; keyword and direction are case\-insensitive (\fBFLOWCHART td\fR, \fBGraph LR\fR). Without a direction the graph is \fBLR\fR.
.IP \(bu
Node ids are letters, digits and \fB_\fR, Unicode letters included (\fBBüro[Amt]\fR is the node \fBBüro\fR; 0.4).
.IP \(bu
Nodes \fBA\fR, \fBA[box]\fR, \fBA(rounded)\fR, \fBA([stadium])\fR, \fBA((circle))\fR, \fBA{diamond}\fR, \fBA{{hexagon}}\fR, \fBA[(cylinder)]\fR, \fBA[[subroutine]]\fR (box).
.IP \(bu
Edges \fB\-\->\fR, \fB\-\-\-\fR, \fB\-.\->\fR, \fB\-.\-\fR, \fB==>\fR, \fB===\fR, \fB\-\-o\fR, \fB\-\-x\fR, with a label as \fB\-\->|text|\fR, \fB\-\- text \-\->\fR, \fB\-. text .\->\fR or \fB== text ==>\fR; chains \fBA \-\-> B \-\-> C\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fB&\fR joins nodes on either side of an edge: \fBA & B \-\-> C & D\fR gives one edge for every pair (\fBA\->C\fR, \fBA\->D\fR, \fBB\->C\fR, \fBB\->D\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fBsubgraph id [label]\fR ... \fBend\fR becomes a \fBtudiagram\fR group (nesting allowed); an edge to or from the subgraph id is dropped.
.IP \(bu
\fBstyle\fR, \fBclassDef\fR, \fBclass\fR, \fBclick\fR, \fBlinkStyle\fR are skipped; \fB%%\fR starts a comment; \fB;\fR separates statements, but not inside a label in brackets, an edge label \fB|..|\fR or quotes (\fBA[Jörg;Büro]\fR is one node).
.SS "Supported diagram types"
.PP
Graph\-like types go through \fBparse\fR and then \fBtudiagram\fR. They take the graph options above:
.CS
graph / flowchart       stateDiagram / stateDiagram-v2
requirementDiagram      erDiagram
classDiagram / classDiagram-v2
mindmap                 block-beta          gitGraph
architecture / architecture-beta
C4Context  C4Container  C4Component  C4Dynamic  C4Deployment
.CE
.PP
Non\-graph types are drawn by \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR only. \fBparse\fR raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUFLOW UNSUPPORTED}\fR for them:
.CS
pie                  xychart-beta         quadrantChart
journey              timeline             sankey / sankey-beta
gantt                sequenceDiagram      radar / radar-beta
treemap / treemap-beta
packet / packet-beta kanban
.CE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuflow
namespace import ::tclutils::tuflow::*

set graph {graph LR
    A[Start] --> B{Check}
    B -->|ok| C[Done]
    B -->|no| A
}
writePng $graph flow.png -scale 3
set svg [toSvg $graph]

set pie {pie title Result
    "pass" : 87
    "fail" : 3
}
writePng $pie pie.png -width 640 -height 400 -scale 2 -legend 1
.CE
.PP
\fBexamples/demo\-tuflow.tcl\fR renders a flowchart, a state diagram and a requirement diagram to SVG and PNG. \fBexamples/demo\-tudiagram.tcl\fR builds the model by hand. Both add \fBlib/tm\fR themselves.
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
\fBtoSvg\fR/\fBtoPng\fR on a graph are equivalent to \fBtudiagram::toSvg\fR/\fBtoPng\fR of \fBparse\fR's result; the facade just hides the dispatch. Keeping \fBparse\fR graph\-only means existing callers that want the raw model are unaffected.
.IP \(bu
New non\-graph families are added in one place (a dispatch branch here plus a \fBtu<type>\fR module exposing \fBparse\fR/\fBtoSvg\fR/\fBtoPng\fR); consumers calling the facade need no change.
.IP \(bu
Family modules for graphs: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR, \fBtclutils::tustate\fR, \fBtclutils::turequirement\fR, \fBtclutils::tuer\fR, \fBtclutils::tuclass\fR, \fBtclutils::tumindmap\fR, \fBtclutils::tuc4\fR, \fBtclutils::tublock\fR, \fBtclutils::tugit\fR, \fBtclutils::tuarchitecture\fR. Non\-graph renderers: \fBtclutils::tupie\fR, \fBtclutils::tuxychart\fR, \fBtclutils::tuquadrant\fR, \fBtclutils::tujourney\fR, \fBtclutils::tutimeline\fR, \fBtclutils::tusankey\fR, \fBtclutils::tugantt\fR, \fBtclutils::tusequence\fR, \fBtclutils::turadar\fR, \fBtclutils::tutreemap\fR, \fBtclutils::tupacket\fR, \fBtclutils::tukanban\fR. Backends: \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR, \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUFLOW <REASON>}\fR — \fBUNSUPPORTED\fR (a diagram type with no renderer), \fBEMPTY\fR (no nodes in a flowchart), \fBBADID\fR (a node id is not letters, digits and \fB_\fR: a hyphen after an id is leftover junk, not an edge — e.g. \fBNwifi\-3["SSID"]\fR). Errors from the dispatched family propagate with their own code (\fB{TCLUTILS TUDIAGRAM ...}\fR, \fB{TCLUTILS TUPIE ...}\fR, and the same shape for the other families). A \fB\-scale\fR that is not a positive integer is that family's \fBARG\fR error. A \fB\-fontfile\fR that names a missing file is its \fBFONT\fR error.
